<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of South</p>
<p>American Libertadores Cup first round, group five matches played</p>
<p>on Wednesday:</p>
<p>In Montevideo: Nacional (Uruguay) 2 Penarol (Uruguay) 0</p>
<p>(halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Mario Barilko (75) and Alvaro Recoba (85)</p>
<p>Attendance: 48,000</p>
<p>In Bogota: Millonarios (Colombia) 2 Deportivo Cali</p>
<p>(Colombia) 2 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Millonarios - Ricardo Perez (12), Alex Daza (36)</p>
<p>Deportivo Cali - Walter Escobar (50), Edson Mafla (80)</p>
<p>Attendance: 35,000</p>
<p>Standings</p>
<p> Penarol		 5  3  0  2  8  7  9</p>
<p> Millonarios	   5  2  1  2  8  8  7</p>
<p> Deportivo Cali	3  1  1  1  5  4  4</p>
<p> Nacional		3  1  0  2  4  6  3</p>
<p>Note: top three teams qualify for the second round.</p>
</text>
